                <pb facs="0295" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.01/355: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lawton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-15T13:00:00-05:00">January 15, 1934—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. Department’s telegram No. 1, January 12, 5 p.m. Please inform President Ubico
                    immediately that the Department is informed concerning President Sacasa’s plan,
                    is in sympathy with it, and hopes that President Ubico will agree to it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
